# LINE ENDINGS
#
# Every text file is stored in the repository with LF and checked out with LF,
# on every machine. Without this the repo had no opinion at all: core.autocrlf
# was unset, something had written CRLF into the working tree, and git reported
# 27 files as modified whose diffs were entirely invisible characters. That is
# not cosmetic. It hid real changes in the noise, it made `git add -A` sweep up
# files nobody had touched, and it meant the honest way to see what had actually
# changed was `git diff --ignore-cr-at-eol --numstat`, which nobody remembers.
#
# eol=lf rather than bare `text=auto` on purpose: this repo is edited from a
# Windows machine and from a Linux container, and "whatever the platform
# prefers" is how the two ended up disagreeing in the first place.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binaries, which must never be transformed. `text=auto` detects most of these
# on content, but being explicit costs nothing and a corrupted image is an
# annoying way to learn the detection was wrong.
*.png   binary
*.jpg   binary
*.jpeg  binary
*.gif   binary
*.webp  binary
*.ico   binary
*.pdf   binary
*.woff  binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf   binary
*.tgz   binary
*.zip   binary
